From: REPRO-SIGN reproduction
Subject: Preserve integer beam indices with PyTorch 1.7

PyTorch 1.7 applies true division to integer tensors, so Tensor.div returns a
Float tensor here. index_select requires Long indices and the published code
therefore fails as soon as translation beam size exceeds one. Floor division
preserves the PyTorch 1.4 behavior for these non-negative flattened IDs.

diff --git a/signjoey/search.py b/signjoey/search.py
--- a/signjoey/search.py
+++ b/signjoey/search.py
@@ -354,5 +354,5 @@ def beam_search(
         # reconstruct beam origin and true word ids from flattened order
-        topk_beam_index = topk_ids.div(decoder.output_size)
+        topk_beam_index = topk_ids // decoder.output_size
         topk_ids = topk_ids.fmod(decoder.output_size)
 
         # map beam_index to batch_index in the flat representation
